From 59224abda521fdad3bb052b4aaf45a8a245ea2f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baris Dinc <barisdinc@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:52:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] board: pluto: Add a DVB-S2 beacon to the DATV repeater

The beacon transmits a transport stream file as DVB-S2 QPSK in the lower
part of the output channel, next to the relayed signal:

  ffmpeg -re -stream_loop -1 (remux to a constant rate TS)
    | dvbs2_tx (DVB-S2 + RRC, TX DMA at fs/8 through the FPGA interpolator)
    -> axi_datv_xpdr NCO (shift into the channel) + repeater output

datv_repeater:
- new [DATV] keys: beacon, beacon_file, beacon_sr_ksps, beacon_fec,
  beacon_rolloff, beacon_pilots, beacon_level_dbfs, beacon_offset_khz,
  beacon_name
- with the beacon on, the automatic sample rate is rounded up so that
  fs / 8 is an integer multiple of the symbol rate (333 kS/s: 13.33 MSPS,
  500 kS/s and 1 MS/s: 16 MSPS)
- the encoder pipeline runs in the background and is restarted if it
  exits; the DAC data select is restored because the driver hands the
  DAC back to the DDS when the DMA stops
- warns if the file bit rate exceeds the channel capacity
- status shows the beacon frequency and the encoder settings
- /var/run/datv.conf is read last (runtime settings, not persistent)

datv_beacon start [file] [kS/s] [fec] | stop | status starts and stops
the beacon through /var/run/datv.conf without touching the persistent
configuration.

atolye_beacon.ts is the default beacon: 5 s loop, H.264 640x360 25 fps
280 kbit/s CBR + AAC 48 kbit/s mono, ~400 kbit/s in total, which fits
333 kS/s QPSK 2/3 (440 kbit/s). The beacon is on by default: 500 kS/s
QPSK 2/3, 3 MHz below the TX frequency (5757 MHz).
